 on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Ron DeSantis (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's governorship is open as Ron DeSantis terms out, with Republicans coalescing around Byron Donalds and Democrats nominating David Jolly. The state's rightward drift gives Donalds a structural edge, and he has built a commanding financial lead, holding roughly $33 million more than Jolly entering the final stretch. Mid-October polling averages put Donalds ahead by about four to six points, and betting markets treat him as a clear favorite.\n\nStill, the race shows signs of life for Democrats. A University of North Florida poll in late October found the two effectively tied, the Democratic Governors Association has put $1 million behind Jolly, and Bill Clinton has campaigned with him in South Florida. Questions about Donalds' standing with Latino voters add uncertainty. The balance of evidence points to a narrow but real Republican advantage.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1709, "margin": -5.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2654, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2923, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2636, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1983, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2414, "margin": -3.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2597, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2217, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2584, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.252, "margin": -4.3}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2745, "margin": -3.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2552, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2498, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2281, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2329, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2195, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2688, "margin": -3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2284, "margin":